# Floats have their copies behind the front of a loop where the loop's own text multiplies or divides an element of the holder. Where every product is asked for its factors, more loops
# were built twice, for nothing: elements with several users, multiplied by a whole constant: what is read is being taken apart. Such a product speaks for no floats.
# An element whose ONLY use is a product speaks for them whatever the factor (`s + held[i] * 2`), and so does one with several users that is multiplied by anything else (`v * v`), and a quotient.
# f1 = go
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float32Array|Float64Array|Int16Array|Int32Array|Int8Array|Uint16Array|Uint32Array|Uint8ClampedArray
# CHECK-NOT: builtinClass=Float64Array
# CHECK-NOT: builtinClass=Float32Array
